+### L-brougham-parked-2794 — separate catalogue-guided1904Brougham
+
+**Decision:** Propose one additional empty closed Brougham at localENU E1397.9,N−3240,bearing178.99 in1904, without replacing or branding generic C02. The1893Studebaker catalogue leaf0095 (source `studebaker_1893_illustrated_souvenir`, actual plateSHA256 `b458565ec06ba1e8e59d1455cc2d3f277c2371910b3085c2085749fc59a68abe`) attests a maker/type design before1904. It does not attest this individual vehicle, Chicago/Prairie presence, ownership, a Pullman/Glessner connection or this stop. `belongs_to` remains null.
+
+**Reconstructed:** all absolute metres, unseen sides/interior/construction, material optics, colors as pigment, hardware attachment/strength, pad thickness/hidden opposite-side symmetry and world stand. V14 source geometry has two separated rounded footplates per side and a fixed parked-down paired-team pole with original ground shoe; it is not single-horse shafts or an invented hinge. Only the indexednear is proposed. ExactV14near source/main/published/phone photographs, all actual wheel/shoe/carriageway and body/pole/obstacle clearance, card/pick/tier/disposal and ordinary release checks remain pending; no visual/full-LOD/photographic acceptance is asserted by this entry.
+
+**Unsupported:** occupants, live boarding, doors/steering, horses/hitch coupling/reins, collisions/physics and traffic. Native hitch[0,.037,3.8]m is a parked-down datum, not a usable working-height team interface. Existing30mmwheel-plane bound and Full100m/Balanced65m/Light0 remain unchanged; static shoe guard refuses nonfinite ground, >1mm penetration or >30mmgap on the same rendered surface. No automatic stand move, model tilt, hitch adjustment or hidden fallback qualifies a failed stand.
+
+**Ticket:** T-2794. Photographic/occupied completion remains OPEN.
